    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36-a1">

                <pb facs="1065" n="907" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg907"/>

                <head>[Inclosure.—Translation.]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Province of Leghorn,<lb/>Chamber of Commerce and
                            Arts</hi></placeName>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>It is hereby certified, for the sake of truth, that from time immemorial, the
                    sweet olive oil of Tuscany has always been designated and known—both in Italy
                    and abroad—by the name of “Lucca oil,” and that the reputable firm of Samuel Rae
                    &amp; Co., established here in 1836, leads in the trade, exporting nothing but
                    the best olive oil of Tuscany under the customary name of “Lucca oil.”</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Ardizzone</hi>, <hi
                                    rendition="#italic">President.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Barsanti</hi>, <hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Leghorn</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic">September 29,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
